+++ b/docs/a3-tmr-local-task-boundaries.md
@@ -18,4 +18,12 @@ Core selection, early-resolve marks, dispatch queues, and ACK handling are
-unchanged. Predicated, sync-start, MIX, idle, and unmarked entries retain their
-existing fallback. Only a selected gated handoff prepares arguments on AICPU;
-other gated tasks prepare them on the waiting AICore as usual. Ready tasks
-retain their CPU-prepared arguments.
+unchanged. A gated idle core may execute its checked Scalar prefix before its
+full-fanin doorbell; its local Wait has no predecessor to drain. A `sync_start`
+successor also permits the prefix, while the unchanged cohort doorbell still
+holds computation until every member owns its running slot and all inputs are
+ready. Pending handoffs publish the local FIN before waiting for that doorbell,
+so the original pending-to-running promotion can complete the rendezvous.
+
+Predicated, MIX, and unmarked entries retain their existing fallback. Only a
+selected gated pending handoff prepares arguments on AICPU; other gated tasks
+prepare them on the waiting AICore as usual. Ready tasks retain their
+CPU-prepared arguments. Neither idle prefix execution nor sync-start coverage
+adds a dispatch trigger or makes an ACK visible ahead of the existing gate.
